# Cache lifetimes for the static export.
#
# Next copies public/ verbatim into out/, and out/ is what gets uploaded, so
# this file arrives at the deploy root where Pages looks for it — the same route
# _redirects beside it already takes. Production was serving max-age=14400 on
# everything, content-hashed assets included, which throws away the one caching
# guarantee a hashed filename buys you.
#
# /_next/static/* is safe to pin for a year because the filenames carry a
# content hash: a changed file is a changed URL, so a cached copy can never go
# stale. `immutable` additionally stops revalidation on reload.
#
# /images/* gets 30 days rather than the same treatment, because those filenames
# are NOT content-hashed. scripts/pull-images.mjs writes each photo to a stable
# path — public/images/cms/<key>.webp — and replaces it in place when the
# picture behind a key changes. Marking those immutable for a year would strand
# a superseded photo in visitors' caches with no way to evict it.
#
# HTML is deliberately absent and therefore uncached. Every page here is a
# static file that gets rewritten on each deploy at the same URL, and the review
# dates and fee figures are the entire point of the site — a cached document is
# a wrong document.

/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/images/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000
